Linux kernel testing for running on WatchGuard T40 (LS1043A)

to run, deploy to usb drive as described in build-and-deploy.sh, then boot using u-boot script:

```shell
usb start
env set kernel_addr_r 0x80080000
env set fdt_addr_r 0x90000000
env set ramdisk_addr_r 0x94000000
load usb 0:1 ${kernel_addr_r} /boot/linux-mainline-69/Image
load usb 0:1 ${fdt_addr_r} /boot/linux-mainline-69/fsl-ls1043a-wgt40.dtb
load usb 0:1 ${ramdisk_addr_r} /boot/initramfs.uImage
env set bootargs console=ttyS0,115200 earlycon=uart8250,mmio,0x21c0500 root=/dev/sdb1 rw rootwait
booti ${kernel_addr_r} ${ramdisk_addr_r} ${fdt_addr_r}
```


NOTE: this is just a test, not a complete solution. 
expect things to miss and not work correctly.


current state:

- [X] generally boots okay, uart console works and boots without crashing
- [X] usb is working and enumerating as expected (what a pain that was)
- [X] SATA ssd is detected and can be mounted
- [X] thermal sensors work (some broken ones still get listed alongside the real ones)
- [X] 88E1545 QUAD Ethernet Phy working (LAN1-4)
  * [X] full GBE?
- [X] AR8035 Ethernet Phy working (WAN)
  * [X] full GBE?
- [X] I2C working
  * [X] RTC -> time is set automatically from hw clock
  * [X] TPM -> /dev/tpm0 present, idk how to test
  * [ ] EEPROM -> ??
- [X] MX25u3235f SPI flash working and readable
- [X] front panel (LEDs, reset button) controllable (via sysfs gpio)


for details, see [here](https://shadow578.github.io/2025/10/03/linux-on-a-watchguard-t40/).

