## Arch Linux ARM installation

to install arch linux ARM64, follow these steps:

- prepare usb stick with ext4 partition:
  - fdisk /dev/sdx
  - g # new partition table
  - n # new partition
  - 1 # partition number 1
  - <enter> # first sector = full disk
  - <enter> # last sector = full disk
  - w # write changes
  - mkfs.ext4 /dev/sdx1
- download generic arm64 arch from https://archlinuxarm.org/platforms/armv8/generic and extract to ext4 formatted usb drive as per instructions
- convert initramfs to uImage: 
  - mkimage -A arm -O linux -T ramdisk -C none -n "initramfs" -d boot/initramfs-linux.img boot/initramfs-linux.uImage
- run build-and-deploy.sh from linux fork (wgt40 branch) to deploy kernel, dtb and kernel modules to the usb drive
- boot from usb using u-boot command line below, then login as root
- format internal ssd and create a single ext4 partition on it (see usb stick prep above)
- mount internal ssd and copy contents of usb drive to it
  - mkdir /mnt/ssd && mkdir /mnt/usb 
  - mount /dev/sda1 /mnt/ssd
  - mount /dev/sdb1 /mnt/usb
  - cp -a /mnt/usb/* /mnt/ssd/
  - alternativ: dd if=/dev/sdb1 of=/dev/sda1 bs=4M status=progress
- after first ssd boot, init pacman keyring as per guide
- prevent automatic kernel changes updates, add "IgnorePkg = linux*" to /etc/pacman.conf
- add initramfs regenerate hook

### u-boot command line for usb boot

```
usb start
env set kernel_addr_r 0x80080000
env set fdt_addr_r 0x90000000
env set ramdisk_addr_r 0x94000000
load usb 0:1 ${kernel_addr_r} /boot/Image.wgt40
load usb 0:1 ${fdt_addr_r} /boot/fsl-ls1043a-wgt40.dtb
load usb 0:1 ${ramdisk_addr_r} /boot/initramfs-linux.uImage
env set bootargs console=ttyS0,115200 earlycon=uart8250,mmio,0x21c0500 root=/dev/sdb1 rw rootwait
booti ${kernel_addr_r} ${ramdisk_addr_r} ${fdt_addr_r}
```

### u-boot command line for scsi boot

install (SysA setup to boot arch, SysB dumps to u-boot console)
```
env set kernel_addr_r 0x80080000
env set fdt_addr_r 0x90000000
env set ramdisk_addr_r 0x94000000
env set boot_linux "<boot command here>"
env set wgBootSysA "run boot_linux"
env set wgBootSysB "true"
env set bootdelay 3
env save
reset
```

boot command (replace newlines with "; " for install)
```
echo "Booting..."
74lv164 high
scsi scan
74lv164 qb 0
load scsi 0:1 ${kernel_addr_r} /boot/Image.wgt40
74lv164 qc 0
load scsi 0:1 ${fdt_addr_r} /boot/fsl-ls1043a-wgt40.dtb
74lv164 qd 0
load scsi 0:1 ${ramdisk_addr_r} /boot/initramfs-linux.uImage
74lv164 qa 0
env set bootargs console=ttyS0,115200 earlycon=uart8250,mmio,0x21c0500 root=/dev/sda1 rw rootwait
booti ${kernel_addr_r} ${ramdisk_addr_r} ${fdt_addr_r}
```


### Front Panel CLI

a tool for interacting with the front panel is included in _wg-t40/frontpanel.py.
sample services to use ATTN led for bootup status are included as well.


